        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Great Despair"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(aura, emotion, enchantment, fear, incapacitation, mental, occult)\n\n30 feet. Living creatures are frightened 1 while in an ice mummy's great despair aura. They can't naturally recover from this fear while in the area but recover instantly once they leave it. When a creature first enters the area, it must succeed at a 24 Will save (after taking the penalty from being frightened) or be paralyzed for 1d4 rounds. The creature is then temporarily immune for 24 hours."
            },
            "id": "197aac88-09f6-4461-a71a-7ddc79f3948a",
